{
  "version": 8,
  "title": "Daily Summary",
  "description": "The end-of-day review (span `day_summary.generate`, service meridian-rust). ONE centralised LLM call reads the day's evidence (`day_evidence.collect`) and answers with a headline, a narrative, a few insights, and either a verdict per PLANNED ticket or a grouping of what an unplanned day was about. The model contributes JUDGEMENT ONLY - it is never asked for a percentage, a count, or a duration, and where the database already settles an outcome (a posted worklog, a linked ticket, a closed ticket) its answer is discarded. Every number on the screen is computed in Rust by `day_evidence::adherence`.\n\nWHAT TO WATCH: `fallback` is the report card - it means the call failed or the answer was not JSON at all, so the day lost its prose (the plan ledger survives, being computed). `certain_matches` against `plan_items` is the other one: it is how much of the ledger rests on facts rather than on the model's reading, and a collapse there usually means worklog posting or ticket linking has broken upstream, not that the summary has.\n\nThere is no repair loop, on purpose: a second call would double a ~1 minute action's latency. Each row's full trace carries the llm.request(prompt+input)/llm.response(output) subspans. Click a row for the trace.",
  "variables": {
    "list": [],
    "showDynamicFilters": true
  },
  "defaultDatetimeDuration": {
    "type": "relative",
    "relativeTimePeriod": "24h"
  },
  "tabs": [
    {
      "tabId": "default",
      "name": "Default",
      "panels": [
        {
